cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Aegis Coupled-Bound Search (ACBS)"
abstract: >-
  An exact point-to-point shortest-path implementation for weighted directed
  road graphs. Forward and reverse frontiers advance under one shared proof of
  optimality, with a balanced admissible potential and an adaptive scheduler.
  Measured on real OpenStreetMap road networks for Tokyo and Osaka, it returned
  exact shortest paths on every query and finished ahead of bidirectional
  Dijkstra on both a distance metric and a travel-time metric. The size of the
  advantage depends on how much information the geographic lower bound carries,
  so this is not a general superiority claim.
type: software
